cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  schematic2netlist: hand-drawn circuit schematics to SPICE netlists,
  with a verified connectivity benchmark
message: >-
  If you use this software or the connectivity ground truth, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Junaid
    given-names: Ammaar
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE-ME/schematic2netlist"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, fully local pipeline that converts photographs of
  hand-drawn analog circuit schematics into simulation-ready SPICE netlists,
  released with a human-verified connectivity ground truth for the
  Digitize-HCD dataset. The ground truth covers 192 circuits (2,564
  components, 5,090 terminals, 1,497 nets); every net was traced from null
  rather than bootstrapped from pipeline output, and the per-image
  adjudication record is released so each netlist is reproducible from its
  decisions. On the held-out split the pipeline reaches 0.516 strict
  end-to-end success, 0.877 net F1 and 0.182 normalized graph edit distance,
  and a ledgered design-intent repair layer raises DC solvability from 0.526
  to 0.729 without altering any component net assignment.
keywords:
  - circuit digitization
  - hand-drawn schematics
  - netlist extraction
  - SPICE
  - graph extraction
  - document analysis
  - benchmark
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Digitize-HCD: A dataset for digitization of handwritten circuit diagrams"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ahmed
        given-names: N.
    doi: 10.17632/rngcz5wtv8
    year: 2025
    notes: Source image corpus, CC BY 4.0.
  - type: data
    title: "CGHD: A dataset of circuit graphs from hand-drawn diagrams"
    url: "https://zenodo.org/records/10056817"
    notes: Cross-dataset zero-shot material, CC BY 4.0.
